xBRZ ("Scale by rules", Zenju), from the HqMAME project.  The files' own
notice says "GNU General Public License" without naming a version (so any
version may be chosen, as GPL-2 section 9 provides), with the HqMAME/MAME
linking exception; PPSSPP ships this same code in its GPL-2.0-or-later
emulator.  Here it is used under the GPL version 2, like the rest of the
app.

Taken from PPSSPP's ext/xbrz (which reads/writes R in the low byte, the
byte order of this port's RGBA8 textures).  Changes, all marked "GBAdhoc":
  - the 64 MB colour-distance table is 2 MB (sources are RGB565), built by
    xbrz::init() instead of a guarded function-local static;
  - single precision instead of double;
  - makePixel() writes an opaque pixel;
  - no <vector>, no PPSSPP headers;
  - scaleRect: a rectangle of the source (rows and columns), optionally
    written at any place and row pitch of a larger target.
